cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenSylab in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "OpenSylab LIMS"
abstract: >-
  Open-source Laboratory Information Management System for medical diagnostics,
  with a tamper-evident ISO 15189-oriented audit trail (HMAC-SHA256 hash chain),
  RBAC, MFA/TOTP, and native HL7 v2.5.1 + FHIR R4 support. Self-hosted, C++17
  backend with an embedded SQLite database and a React/TypeScript frontend.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "AurevionSec"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AurevionSec/openSylab"
url: "https://github.com/AurevionSec/openSylab"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-05"
keywords:
  - LIMS
  - medical-diagnostics
  - ISO-15189
  - audit-trail
  - HL7
  - FHIR
  - RBAC
  - self-hosted
